          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Iran war drives datacenter construction costs up 20% as supply chains fracture globally",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "The ongoing Iran war is disrupting global datacenter construction supply chains, with the British Computer Society reporting that builders are facing material cost increases of up to 20% alongside patchy delivery schedules for critical components. The disruption threatens to delay AI infrastructure buildout at a time when hyperscalers are racing to commission new compute capacity. The supply chain strain has global implications, affecting projects from the Gulf region to Europe and beyond.",
            "url": "https://www.theregister.com/on-prem/2026/05/08/iran-war-disrupts-datacenter-construction-supply-chains-raises-material-costs/5235852",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
